LHG 5 AC Based devices platform is  based on the Qualcomm Atheros IPQ4018 used in various MikroTik wireless devices with 802.11a/n/ac radio, 1x 10/100/1000 Mbps Gigabit Ethernet port, 16 MB SPI NOR flash and 256 MB RAM DDR3. It comprises the following Mikrotik devices:

* [[https://mikrotik.com/product/lhg_5_ac|LHG 5 AC]] (RBLHGG-5acD)

* [[https://mikrotik.com/product/lhg_xl_5_ac|LHG XL 5 AC]] (RBLHGG-5acD-XL)

* [[https://mikrotik.com/product/sxtsq_5_ac|SXTsq 5AC]] (RBSXTsqG-5acD)

* [[https://mikrotik.com/product/disc_lite5_ac|Disc Lite5 AC]] (RBDiscG-5acD)

* [[https://mikrotik.com/product/ldf_5_ac|LDF5 AC]] (RBLDFG-5acD) NOT SUPPORTED YET BY OPENWRT!!!

They all share the same PCB, just the hardware name changes. The instructions and descriptions given in this entry are valid for all these devices (and possibly many more)



